---
// Determinacy ladder with length controls, plus task-naming refusal share. Rung values from runs/determinacy_summary.json; task-naming shares from the protocol record.
---

<figure class="diagram measure determinacy-ladder">
  <div class="diagram-scroll">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 428" role="img" aria-labelledby="determinacy-ladder-title determinacy-ladder-desc">
    <title id="determinacy-ladder-title">Compliance against how much of the answer is specified in advance</title>
    <desc id="determinacy-ladder-desc">Upper panel: refusal falls to minus 0.175 at two named structural elements, then returns to minus 0.025 at a full template. Lower panel: the share of refusals that name the requested task rises from 40 to 58 to 72 percent across the same rungs.</desc>
    <text x="16.0" y="26.0" font-family="'Geist', system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13.5" fill="#435347" text-anchor="start" font-weight="600">Specifying the answer buys compliance, up to a point</text>
    <text x="16.0" y="46.0" font-family="'Geist', system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#56665A" text-anchor="start">Then it collapses, because spelling out the output spells out the request.</text>
