    <text x="498.0" y="400.0" font-family="'Geist', system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="#435347" text-anchor="middle">empty slots</text>
    <text x="498.0" y="416.0" font-family="'Geist', system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="9" fill="#56665A" text-anchor="middle">r4</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption><span class="figure-title">Completion determinacy is a lever with a peak.</span> Top: change in refusal rate against a 90.5% reference, with ± MDE whiskers. Hollow triangles are length-matched padding at the two long rungs; they move nothing, so the collapse is not about prompt length. Bottom: the share of refusals that explicitly name the requested task rather than declining generically, measured at three rungs. Over-specifying the output over-specifies the request: the peak is at two named elements, and the full template is no better than saying nothing at all.</figcaption>
</figure>
